          "filename": "Athens - National Archeological Museum - Zeus (or Poseidon) statue - 20060930.jpg",
          "caption": "Bronze Sculpture, thought to be either Poseidon or Zeus (Poseidon is more probable), circa460 BC, National Archaeological Museum, Athens. This masterpiece of classical sculpture was found by fishermen in their nets off the coast of Cape Artemisium in 1928. It is one of the few preserved original statues of the Severe Style. The figure is more than 2 m in height.",
